WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.777
My ship sails in the morning from the port of Lagos, Portugal.

2
00:00:04.778 --> 00:00:14.051
I’m supervising my sailors as they lower crates into the cargo area, check the sails for tears and holes, and test the ropes.

3
00:00:14.052 --> 00:00:22.929
India is our destination, by order of Prince Henry of Portugal, and we will be exploring seas we’ve never seen before.

4
00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:34.526
My name is Edmundo Veloso. The year is 1434, and I have just been promoted to captain of the Terra Nova , a ship both fast and

5
00:00:34.527 --> 00:00:42.137
true. I am full of curiosity and armed with tools that have served mariners for years and years and the latest

6
00:00:42.138 --> 00:00:46.077
charts. This is the opportunity I’ve been working

7
00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:54.834
for. I first set foot on a ship at age 12 when, without warning, my father took me to the docks and set me up as an apprentice on a

8
00:00:54.835 --> 00:01:00.374
ship. I came from a big family, and my father could not afford to feed

9
00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:05.076
everyone. So over the next twenty years, I learned everything about

10
00:01:05.077 --> 00:01:08.596
sailing. I swabbed the decks and polished the

11
00:01:08.597 --> 00:01:12.839
brass. I learned how to rig the sails, navigate, and steer the

12
00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:19.859
ship. Climbing the rigging like a monkey to set the sails was more than a job for me; it was the most fun I ever

13
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:25.174
had. The crow’s nest, high atop the highest mast, was my favorite

14
00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:32.479
place. Although I was not enchanted with the sea as a child, I became enchanted as I grew up on

15
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:37.275
it. The reign of Prince Henry of Portugal is an exciting time to be a

16
00:01:37.276 --> 00:01:44.289
mariner. Henry’s goal is to find a sea route to India by heading south along the west coast of

17
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:50.883
Africa. A man of science, Prince Henry wants to find a faster route to trade for spices and precious metals from the

18
00:01:50.884 --> 00:01:56.485
East, to spread Christianity, and perhaps even to discover new fishing

19
00:01:56.486 --> 00:01:59.507
grounds. The port of Lagos is close to Prince Henry’s

20
00:01:59.508 --> 00:02:06.922
villa, where I had dinner a few nights ago and met cartographers, astrologers, navigators, and other

21
00:02:06.923 --> 00:02:12.020
explorers. It was an inspiring evening, and I came to understand Henry’s

22
00:02:12.021 --> 00:02:19.994
plan—to use scientific methods in exploration and publish our findings for the benefit of those who come after us.

23
00:02:19.995 --> 00:02:27.232
Among the tools I use to navigate are the nocturnal, the astrolabe, and the mariner’s compass.

24
00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:30.476
The nocturnal allows me to determine the time at night.

25
00:02:30.477 --> 00:02:35.214
I locate the Big Dipper, stars in an easy-to-see constellation.

26
00:02:35.215 --> 00:02:41.731
Two of its stars line up and point to the North Star—that’s why they’re called pointer stars. I

27
00:02:41.732 --> 00:02:46.593
line up the hole in the center of my nocturnal with the North Star. Then

28
00:02:46.594 --> 00:02:54.225
I swing the long arm of the nocturnal until it lines up with the Big Dipper’s pointer stars and read the time! With

29
00:02:54.226 --> 00:03:01.127
the astrolabe I find my position by measuring how high the noon sun is over the horizon. From

30
00:03:01.128 --> 00:03:08.102
that measurement I can determine latitude—how far north or south our ship is from the equator. My

31
00:03:08.103 --> 00:03:17.217
mariner’s compass has a magnetized needle that points north, which also helps me determine my position—along with my sea charts of course.

32
00:03:17.218 --> 00:03:23.387
These charts have lines that have been drawn to show the direction of the winds, as well as descriptions of landmarks,

33
00:03:23.388 --> 00:03:26.649
which I also use to figure out where I am.

34
00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.690
I keep a record of the time I sail on each bearing (direction) on the compass.

35
00:03:31.691 --> 00:03:39.153
With this method, my tools, and my years of experience, I navigate with certainty on the open seas.

36
00:03:39.154 --> 00:03:44.892
Seven years ago I was the first mate on the ship that discovered the Azores Islands.

37
00:03:44.893 --> 00:03:54.189
Having no land in sight was worrisome since we couldn’t rely on our sea charts, but the results were well worth it—discovering a new land!

38
00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:58.248
Tomorrow we will sail south along the African coast.

39
00:03:58.249 --> 00:04:06.727
My ship, a caravel, carries different types of sails, which will allow us to maneuver easily and quickly in the wind.

40
00:04:06.728 --> 00:04:12.961
Long, thin, and shallow, the caravel is exceptional for exploring the coasts.

41
00:04:12.962 --> 00:04:17.396
It has taken time to assemble my crew of twenty, but they are ready.

42
00:04:17.397 --> 00:04:23.087
Many of them are young men who remind me of myself at that age—full of excitement.

43
00:04:23.088 --> 00:04:29.248
These young sailors are apprehensive, but their curiosity and sense of adventure overcome their fear.

44
00:04:29.249 --> 00:04:35.540
The older men are experienced, and because of this, they know the sea is unforgiving.

45
00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:38.329
They realize the weather can change in a moment.

46
00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:41.647
One morning the sky can be blue and the sea calm.

47
00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:49.465
But by noon a storm might arise, creating giant waves that can capsize any ship.

48
00:04:49.466 --> 00:04:53.314
All my men are superstitious and fearful at times.

49
00:04:53.315 --> 00:05:02.275
For instance, some believe the farther south one sails, the hotter the water becomes, because the sea gets colder as one sails northward.

50
00:05:02.276 --> 00:05:06.031
They fear southern seas will boil them.

51
00:05:06.032 --> 00:05:14.865
Others believe we will reach the edge of the earth and fall off, or that monsters lurk in the deep, just waiting for an unsuspecting ship.

52
00:05:14.866 --> 00:05:19.717
Many who have families are not willing to take the risk of a long sea voyage.

53
00:05:19.718 --> 00:05:27.015
I respect their fears because, in fact, I am not immune to them now that I have a family of my own.

54
00:05:27.016 --> 00:05:32.250
But to me this trip is the climax of my career.

55
00:05:32.251 --> 00:05:39.463
I tell the crew of my pride in being on the first ship to sight the Azores and how this trip will be just as memorable,

56
00:05:39.464 --> 00:05:43.362
but in the end, I release anyone who is hesitant.

57
00:05:43.363 --> 00:05:48.004
In uncharted waters I will need commitment not fear.

58
00:05:48.005 --> 00:05:55.029
I will need collaboration not dissent. I will need boldness to face whatever we may have to face.

59
00:05:55.030 --> 00:06:02.209
And so my crew is mostly young, with a few adventurous old sailors who will help me guide us to safe harbors.

60
00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:08.431
We are poised at the beginning of a voyage of discovery. What will the outcome be?

61
00:06:08.432 --> 00:06:19.728
Will we come back triumphant with charts of new shores to add to Prince Henry’s fame, or will we never be heard from again?

